er market you have that 50% increase in Odyle Energy that lets you claim rewards, this seems huge to me.\nThis is from Web AI on what you get paying for a Sub:\nMarketplace Access: Full, unrestricted use of the player auction house to buy and sell gear and materials.\nCurrency Exchange: Direct access to the Kinah ↔ Quna currency exchange to trade in-game wealth for premium currency.\nDirect Trading: The ability to trade items directly with other players on your server\nRemote Storage: Access to account and server storage from anywhere in the world without visiting an NPC. (This one is a HUGE perk)\nWind Breeze Merchant: Access to a special mobile shop for buying consumables.\nOdyle Energy Boost: A 50% faster recharge rate and increased maximum cap for Odyle Energy, which is used for gathering and running dungeons. (This one is also a HUGE perk)\nDoubled PvE Rewards: Doubles the Odyle Energy Cube selection from dungeons, effectively cutting your required run time in half by giving double the loot per run\nI think that's all worth a mere $15 a month. So if you do not have a Sub then you get none or can't do any of the above at all.\n\nLast edited by dizzy99; Sep 28 @ 8:24am\n\nTyra Image: has AION 2\n\nSep 28 @ 7:31am \n\n ImageReport this post\n\nIf a game looks and feels interesting enough i usually sub. Feels fair to me and then I don't have this \"I'd be more efficient if i subbed \" feeling. It also reigns in my game-hopping a bit when I commit by subscription.\nHere it was an easy decision because of the launch scale test , I can be relatively sure my PC handles it and I was sad when the test was over, so i will start wednesday and then decide after the 30 days that come with the founder pack. I also want to play more than one character because I cannot decide between classes and a sub should make that easier too.\nBut i don't see much alternatives around that interest me, so i will probably get one after aswell.\n\nDate Posted: Sep 28 @ 12:08am\n\nPosts: 7-----